Ma Rainey's Black Bottom is a 2020 American drama film directed by George C.

12
00:41:46,666 --> 00:41:52,666
Wolfe and written by Ruben Santiago-Hudson, based on the
1982 play of the same name by August Wilson.

13
00:45:15,555 --> 00:45:21,555
The film stars Viola Davis, Chadwick Boseman, Glynn
Turman, Colman Domingo, and Michael Potts.

14
00:48:44,444 --> 00:48:50,444
Inspired by the career of blues singer Ma Rainey, the film
dramatizes a turbulent recording session in 1920s Chicago.

15
00:52:13,333 --> 00:52:19,333
Produced by Denzel Washington, Todd Black, and Dany Wolf, the project was originally announced
alongside Washington's Fences in 2013 as part of his ten-picture deal with HBO.

16
00:55:42,222 --> 00:55:48,222
The adaptation eventually moved to Netflix and
filming began in Pittsburgh in 2019.

17
00:59:11,111 --> 00:59:17,111
Boseman died during post-production in August 2020, making
Black Bottom his final film appearance.

18
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
The film is dedicated to his memory.

19
01:06:08,888 --> 01:06:14,888
Ma Rainey's Black Bottom began a limited theatrical release on November 25,
2020, before beginning to stream on Netflix on December 18.

20
01:09:37,777 --> 01:09:43,777
Critics praised the performances of Davis, Boseman, and Turman as
well as the costume design and production values.

21
01:13:06,666 --> 01:13:12,666
It was named as one of the ten best films of 2020
by the American Film Institute.

22
01:16:35,555 --> 01:16:41,555
The film received five nominations at the 93rd Academy Awards, including Best Actor (for Boseman),
Best Actress (for Davis), and won two awards: Makeup and Hairstyling and Costume Design.

23
01:20:04,444 --> 01:20:10,444
Additionally, the film received eight Critics' Choice Movie Award nominations and nine NAACP Image Award
nominations, including Outstanding Motion Picture, with Davis and Boseman both winning lead acting awards.

24
01:23:33,333 --> 01:23:39,333
Davis and Boseman also won lead acting awards for their performances at the Screen Actors Guild Awards, making them the first African-American actors in history to win in
leading categories in the same year; both received nominations at the Golden Globes, with Boseman posthumously winning Best Actor – Motion Picture Drama.

25
